Sin Morralla — Proprietary license. All rights reserved.

Copyright (c) 2026 VictorLaraL, author of Sin Morralla. All rights reserved.

This repository is NOT free or open-source software. The repository being public does not grant any license.

1. Scope. The source code of the server, the website, the owner portal and the firmware; the documentation; the
   designs, diagrams, images and texts; the name "Sin Morralla", its logos and its visual identity (together, the
   "Work").

2. Not permitted. Without the author's prior written permission, no one may use, copy, reproduce, modify, adapt,
   translate, compile, run, deploy, distribute, publish, sublicense, sell or otherwise exploit the Work or any part
   of it, or create derivative works from it, whether for profit or not. This includes using the Work to build, train
   or improve products or services, one's own or anyone else's.

3. Trademarks. The name "Sin Morralla" and its logos identify the project and its author. No right to use them is
   granted.

4. The only things permitted.
   a) Reviewing the repository and the public demo to evaluate the project within Hackatón México 2026, to the extent
      and for the period set by that competition's rules.
   b) Viewing the repository and forking it within GitHub, solely as required by GitHub's Terms of Service. That
      permission does not authorize any other use of the Work.

5. Third-party components. Third-party components keep their own licenses and are not part of the Work for the
   purposes of this license; for example, qrcode-generator 1.4.4 (MIT license, in web/vendor) and the development
   dependencies listed in package.json.

6. No warranty. The Work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The author is not liable for any damage
   arising from viewing it or from any unauthorized use.

To request permission to use the Work, open an issue in the repository or contact the author at
https://github.com/VictorLaraL.
